1
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:26,000
As the countdown begins for the new millennium there is
still one number you can always count on.

2
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:46,000
The World Is Not Enough is a adventure, action,
thriller film directed by Michael Apted.

3
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:06,000
Greed, revenge, world dominance and high-tech terrorism – it's all in a day's work for Bond,
who's on a mission to protect a beautiful oil heiress from a notorious terrorist.

4
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:26,000
In a race against time that culminates in a dramatic submarine showdown, Bond works to defuse the
international power struggle that has the world's oil supply hanging in the balance.

5
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:46,000
James Bond, played by Pierce Brosnan.

6
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:06,000
Elektra, played by Sophie Marceau.

7
00:37:20,000 --> 00:37:26,000
Renard, played by Robert Carlyle.

8
00:42:40,000 --> 00:42:46,000
Christmas Jones, played by Denise Richards.

9
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
Valentin Zukovsky, played by Robbie Coltrane.

10
00:53:20,000 --> 00:53:26,000
M, played by Judi Dench.

11
00:58:40,000 --> 00:58:46,000
The World Is Not Enough is a 1999 action spy film, the nineteenth in the James Bond series produced by Eon
Productions and the third to star Pierce Brosnan as the fictional MI6 agent James Bond.

12
01:04:00,000 --> 01:04:06,000
It was directed by Michael Apted, from an original story and
screenplay by Neal Purvis, Robert Wade, and Bruce Feirstein.

13
01:09:20,000 --> 01:09:26,000
It was produced by Michael G.

14
01:14:40,000 --> 01:14:46,000
Wilson and Barbara Broccoli.

15
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
The title is the translation of the motto on the Bond family coat of
arms, first seen in On Her Majesty's Secret Service.

16
01:25:20,000 --> 01:25:26,000
The film's plot revolves around the murder of billionaire businessman Sir Robert King by the terrorist Renard, and Bond's
subsequent assignment to protect King's daughter Elektra, who was previously held for ransom by Renard.

17
01:30:40,000 --> 01:30:46,000
During his assignment, Bond unravels a scheme to increase petroleum prices
by triggering a nuclear meltdown in the waters of Istanbul.

18
01:36:00,000 --> 01:36:06,000
Filming locations included Spain, France, Azerbaijan, Turkey, and
the UK, with interiors shot at Pinewood Studios.

19
01:41:20,000 --> 01:41:26,000
Despite receiving mixed reviews from critics, with the plot and Denise Richards' casting frequently targeted for criticism,
The World Is Not Enough earned over $361 million worldwide, becoming the eighth highest-grossing film of 1999.

20
01:46:40,000 --> 01:46:46,000
It was also the first Eon-produced Bond film officially released by the mainline
Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer label instead of United Artists, the franchise's original owner and distributor.

21
01:52:00,000 --> 01:52:06,000
The World Is Not Enough was followed by Die Another Day in 2002.

22
01:57:20,000 --> 01:57:26,000
The film explores themes of mission, oil, mi6, heiress, bilbao, spain.

23
02:02:40,000 --> 02:02:46,000
The tone is intense.
